<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elias Peter Hoayek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Elias Hoayek, Elias Peter Huwayyik</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elias Peter Hoayek was Maronite Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> from 1898 to 1931. He led a Lebanese delegation to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-conference-1919-1920">Paris Peace Conference</a> in 1919, asking for an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> enlarged beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a> under French protection. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s creation of Greater Lebanon in 1920, adding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a>, Tripoli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidon">Sidon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beqaa-valley">Beqaa Valley</a>, largely met his demands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elias-peter-hoayek.jpg" alt="Elias Peter Hoayek" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elias_Peter_Hoayek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
